{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1792573081","published":"2026-10-21T08:58:08Z","modified":"2026-11-27T16:32:04.300227290Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-96275","CVE-2026-96280"],"summary":"flatpak: Fix of 2 CVEs","details":"- Rebase onto the vendor 1.12.9-4.el9_8.4 sources, which prevent an arbitrary\n  write as root via extra-data extraction (CVE-2026-96275) and harden the OCI\n  delta parser against size overflow (CVE-2026-96280)\n- Retained the TuxCare hardening of regenerate_ld_cache() in\n  common/flatpak-run.c and of flatpak_switch_symlink_and_remove() in\n  common/flatpak-utils.c, which the vendor sources still lack\n- The TuxCare duplicate of the data-dir and /var symlink hardening for\n  common/flatpak-run.c plus the libglnx chase prerequisites is dropped; the\n  vendor's run-harden-ensure-data-dir-and-var-setup-against-symlink-attacks,\n  chase-add-internal-glnx-chaseat-full-for-a-strategic-callback and\n  chase-add-glnx-chase-and-mkdirat patches carry the same fix\n- Keep the retry of openat2() on EAGAIN in libglnx glnx_chaseat(), which\n  the dropped TuxCare patch carried and the vendor's chase patches leave out\n- The TuxCare duplicate for revokefs/writer.c is dropped; the vendor's\n  revokefs-avoid-symlink-path-traversal-* patches carry the same fix","affected":[{"package":{"name":"flatpak","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.8","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/flatpak?distro=almalinux-9.8"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.12.9-4.el9_8.4.tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/tuxcare9.8esu/CLSA-2026-1792573081.json"}},{"package":{"name":"flatpak-devel","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.8","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/flatpak-devel?distro=almalinux-9.8"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.12.9-4.el9_8.4.tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/tuxcare9